<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    OstrichChallenge - Loot

    THE ARMOURY. The basement holds the hotel's only T5 hardened chest, and it is the one place in
    the building that hands the guard a real weapon. Everything here is GUARANTEED, not rolled,
    because the finale is balanced around having it: the same armoury every run.

    Written the way Area 7 does its T4 crucible, appending to the chest's own loot group. Vanilla
    splits that group into numbered sub-groups (groupHardenedChestT5_01 for ammo, _02 weapons and
    armour, _03 medical and so on) and rolls them with count="all", so appending to the PARENT
    adds our items alongside its normal contents rather than competing with them.

    QUALITY, and this took two goes. quality="6" on an ITEM does nothing: in vanilla that attribute
    only ever appears inside <qualitytemplate> blocks. Quality comes from loot_quality_template,
    and that is an attribute of a LOOTGROUP, never of an item. So the rifle gets its own one-item
    group carrying vanilla's qualTwitchT6Template, which is level="1,999999" default_quality="6",
    a fixed 6 at any player level, and the chest references that group.

    Every item id below is checked against the game's items.xml. gunMGT1AK47 is the only AK in the
    game; there is no plain "ammo762mmBullet", the ball round is ammo762mmBulletBall.

    NOTE this group is the game's, so any other T5 hardened chest in the city carries these too.
    In Occupancy that hardly matters, since the player cannot leave the hotel until the run is
    over, but it is worth knowing before this file is reused anywhere else.
-->
<configs>

    <!-- ============================================================
         CONTAINERS SURVIVE BEING SEARCHED (v0.57.2)

         Vanilla destroys many containers on close: rubbish piles vanish as you search them, and a
         container that no longer exists can never restock, which is why the hotel's filing
         cabinets and rubbish were not coming back while ordinary boxes were.

         Area 7 and the Hospital both do exactly this, and it is the piece that was missing here:
         strip destroy_on_close from EVERY loot container, then put it back as "empty" on junk and
         laundry baskets so those collapse to an empty version rather than disappearing entirely.
         ============================================================ -->
    <!-- ============================================================
         v1.96.0: NO VEHICLE CRAFTING MAGAZINES ANYWHERE IN LOOT.

         Fril, 8 Oct 2026: "I think we should remove all vehiclesSkillsMagazines from loot and
         remove the Grease Monkey skill tree. Putting points in there is pointless as you cannot
         craft any vehicles?"

         HIS PREMISE IS CORRECT AND THIS MOD ALREADY SAID SO IN TWO PLACES. recipes.xml removes
         all twelve vehicle recipes, and progression.xml's own header reads "a mod where no
         vehicle can be crafted at all". The 4x4 is spawned by the DLL, is indestructible, and
         needs no fuel, battery or repair, so nothing about the escape depends on this either.

         ONE REMOVE, FIFTEEN PLACES. vehiclesSkillMagazine appears in fifteen vanilla lootgroups:
         skillMagazines, groupQuestRewardSkillMagazinesAll01, groupChallengeRewardSkillMagazinesAll01,
         groupCars02, groupGarage, groupGarage02, groupRollingToolbox03, groupMoPower02,
         groupFarmTruck, groupFarmTruck02, groupPassNGasMagazines, groupPassNGas01, groupZpackLab02,
         groupZpackSoldier02 and groupZpackThug02. RemoveByXPath iterates every match rather than
         taking the first, which was read out of the 3.3 IL on 8 Oct, so one line does the lot.

         THE IMPORTANT ONE IS skillMagazines. That is the general pool the Book Bag draws its
         "1,3" from, and three of the zpack lists are what the guests' bags pull from, so this
         also stops the magazine arriving through the back door.
         ============================================================ -->
    <remove xpath="//item[@name='vehiclesSkillMagazine']" />

    <removeattribute xpath="//lootcontainer/@destroy_on_close" />
    <setattribute xpath="//lootcontainer[@name='junk']" name="destroy_on_close">empty</setattribute>
    <setattribute xpath="//lootcontainer[@name='laundryBasket']" name="destroy_on_close">empty</setattribute>

    <!-- ============================================================
         THE CHEST IS OUR LIST AND NOTHING ELSE (v1.90.0)

         Fril, 7 Oct: "I think the chest should be our loot only after tonight."

         Until now we APPENDED to vanilla's groupHardenedChestT5, so the chest gave our armoury
         plus everything vanilla's eight sub-groups rolled. That is where the treasure map came
         from, and it was never going to be the last surprise: the parent group pulls from
         sub-groups the mod does not control and TFP can change at any version.

         WHAT IS BEING DROPPED, listed so it is a decision and not an accident:

             _01 count 5   Ammo
             _02 count 2   Weapon OR Armor
             _03 count 1   Medical
             _04 count 1   Mods
             _05 count 2   Books and schematics (perk books, skill magazines)
             _06 count 2   Bonus items
             _07 count 1   Cash and prizes
             _08 count 1   T5 bonus items
             conditional   The Christmas holiday gear roll
             booksAllScaled with the buffPerkBookwormSuccess requirement

         So the chest no longer gives MODS, ARMOUR, PERK BOOKS, SKILL MAGAZINES or the Bookworm
         bonus roll. The hotel still seeds magazines elsewhere (occEssentialMags, see the
         bookshelf work further down this file), so books are not gone from the run, only from
         the chest.

         ORDER MATTERS AND IT IS THE WHOLE TRAP HERE. XML patches apply in document order, and
         our own items are <item> children of the same group. If these removes ran AFTER the
         append below they would delete the armoury along with vanilla's contents and leave an
         empty chest. They are deliberately placed before it. Do not move them.

         The removes are two, not one: the direct <item> children, and the <conditional> block,
         which an "/item" xpath does not reach because its item is nested inside it.
         ============================================================ -->
    <remove xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupHardenedChestT5']/item" />
    <remove xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupHardenedChestT5']/conditional" />

    <!-- The rifle, in its own group so it can carry the fixed-quality template.
         INSERTBEFORE, not insertafter: the loader parses the file in order and a group must be
         DEFINED BEFORE IT IS REFERENCED, or it throws "lootgroup does not exist or has not been
         defined before being referenced" and the whole of loot.xml fails to load. -->
    <insertbefore xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupHardenedChestT5']">
        <lootgroup name="occArmouryRifle" count="1" loot_quality_template="qualTwitchT6Template">
            <item name="gunMGT1AK47" count="1"/>
        </lootgroup>
    </insertbefore>

    <!-- The armoury: a rifle, ammunition for it, and enough medicine to survive using it. -->
    <append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupHardenedChestT5']">
        <item group="occArmouryRifle" count="1"/>
        <item name="ammo762mmBulletBall" count="300"/>
        <item name="medicalFirstAidKit" count="2"/>
        <item name="medicalBandage" count="5"/>
        <item name="drugAntibiotics" count="2"/>
        <item name="drugPainkillers" count="2"/>
        <item name="foodCanChili" count="3"/>
        <item name="foodCanPasta" count="3"/>
        <item name="foodCanBeef" count="2"/>
        <item name="drinkJarBoiledWater" count="4"/>
    </append>

    <!-- ============================================================
         LOOSE ROUNDS, IN MANY PLACES (v0.86.0)

         Fril: "more ammunition in loot but in smaller quantities."

         WHAT THE HOTEL ACTUALLY HELD BEFORE THIS. Counted from the prefab itself rather than
         guessed: Ostrich_Hotel_2.tts is 60x100x60 and holds 1,073 container blocks, 932 of them
         with a loot list, of which 247 can produce 9mm at all. Four types are 209 of that 247:

             luggage     81        toilet      55
             nightstand  48        microwave   25

         And every one of them hides its ammo behind a nested gate: the parent group reaches its
         ammo-bearing sub-group only at veryLow (0.05) or low (0.20), and the sub-group then makes
         ONE weighted pick among ten or so entries. Multiply it out and searching all 209 yields
         about TWELVE rounds. The player starts with thirty. A complete sweep of the entire hotel
         gave back less than half a magazine.

         WHY THIS APPENDS TO THE PARENT AND NOT THE SUB-GROUP. All four parents are count="all",
         so an item appended here rolls INDEPENDENTLY at exactly the probability given. Appending
         to the sub-groups instead would drop our line into a weighted single pick and the real
         rate would depend on the other entries' weights, which is how vanilla's own ammo ends up
         so much rarer than it looks. Same lesson as the honey in traders.xml: go to the level
         where the outcome is bounded.

         THE NUMBERS. 0.10 at 1 to 3 rounds is about 42 rounds per full sweep on top of vanilla's
         twelve, which is roughly three rounds per floor. It reads as "most rooms have nothing,
         and now and then there are a few loose rounds in a bedside drawer". Fril chose it from a
         table of the alternatives; medHigh and above were ruled out because with the two-day loot
         respawn, ammunition would stop being a constraint at all.

         A RATE, NOT A PLACEMENT, ON PURPOSE. The floors are still being decorated, so the
         container counts will keep rising. A probability per container scales with the building;
         hand-placed ammo would have to be redone every time Bunny finishes a floor.

         9mm ONLY, DELIBERATELY. It is the guard's sidearm and the round the run is balanced
         around. 7.62 is the armoury's guaranteed 300 and should stay something you have to go
         down to the basement for, so it is not scattered here.
         ============================================================ -->

    <append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupNightstand']">
        <item name="ammo9mmBulletBall" count="1,3" loot_prob_template="lower"/>
    </append>
    <append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupLuggage']">
        <item name="ammo9mmBulletBall" count="1,3" loot_prob_template="lower"/>
    </append>
    <append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupToilet']">
        <item name="ammo9mmBulletBall" count="1,3" loot_prob_template="lower"/>
    </append>
    <append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupMicrowave']">
        <item name="ammo9mmBulletBall" count="1,3" loot_prob_template="lower"/>
    </append>

    <!-- ============================================================
         ROOM SAFES: THE FIRST CRACK PAYS, THE REFILLS DO NOT

         A locked safe in every room. Getting into one the first time can yield a lockpick, which
         is how a player who started with none ever gets to pick rather than break. Everything
         after that is an ordinary restock: a little ammo, a few Dukes, no picks. Otherwise a
         single safe on a two day timer is an infinite lockpick tap.

         WHY TWO CONTAINERS RATHER THAN ONE. A loot list cannot know whether it has been rolled
         before, so the difference has to live somewhere that persists. It lives on the container:
         the safe starts pointed at occSafeFirst and the DLL repoints it at occSafeRestock once it
         has been opened. lootListName is written to the save (TEFeatureStorage.Write), so the safe
         carries its own memory and the mod needs no record of which safes have been cracked.

         PICKED OR BEATEN, IT LANDS HERE EITHER WAY. TEFeatureLockPickable.DowngradeToUnlockedVariant
         sends a successfully picked safe to the same unlocked block that breaking one produces, so
         both routes open the same container and both get the first-crack roll.

         Appended at the end, after vanilla's own groups are defined: a group must exist before it
         is referenced or the whole file fails to load.
         ============================================================ -->
    <append xpath="/lootcontainers">

        <!-- First time in. Everything a vanilla safe holds, plus the chance of a pick. -->
        <lootcontainer name="occSafeFirst" size="8,5" sound_open="UseActions/open_safe"
                       sound_close="UseActions/close_safe" open_time="1"
                       loot_quality_template="qualPlus1Template">
            <item group="groupSmallSafeLoot"/>
            <item name="resourceLockPick" count="1" prob="0.1"/>
        </lootcontainer>

        <!-- Every refill after that. Ammo, Dukes and the odd bit of safe loot. No picks. -->
        <lootcontainer name="occSafeRestock" size="8,5" sound_open="UseActions/open_safe"
                       sound_close="UseActions/close_safe" open_time="1"
                       loot_quality_template="qualPlus1Template">
            <item group="groupSmallSafeLoot02" loot_prob_template="medHigh" force_prob="true"/>
            <item group="groupSmallSafeLoot03" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
        </lootcontainer>

    </append>

    <!-- ============================================================
         OLD CASH BECOMES DUKES (v0.94.0)

         Fril: Dukes are the primary source of food and drink, because the vending machines are
         the only shop in the building. Vending machines SELL, they do not buy, and there is no
         trader in the hotel, so every note of oldCash in the loot tables was an item the player
         could look at and nothing else. Dead weight in the only economy the run has.

         WHAT THE BUILDING ACTUALLY HELD, counted from the prefab rather than guessed. The current
         Ostrich_Hotel_2.tts is 60x100x60, 66,300 solid blocks, 864 block types and 953 containers
         carrying a loot list. Resolved through every group chain, a complete sweep yields:

             Dukes     279        old cash   674

         And the old cash was where the Dukes should have been. The ten room safes are 434 of that
         674, 65% of it, because groupSmallSafeLoot03 pays in oldCash. The comment above on
         occSafeRestock has said "Ammo, Dukes and the odd bit of safe loot" since it was written
         and that was never true: a safe restock was 43.4 old cash and ZERO Dukes. The repeating
         tap the economy is built on was paying in the one item nothing accepts.

         Dukes before this were also concentrated in exactly the wrong places: 225 of the 279 sat
         in four single containers (the two hardened chests, the till and two hidden stashes), and
         luggage, microwave and the room safes produced none at all.

         THE CHANGE. One line, because oldCash appears in 30 places across the merged config and
         listing them would rot the moment the game patches:

             every <item name="oldCash"> anywhere in loot.xml becomes casinoCoin

         COUNTS LEFT ALONE, Fril's call. Note this is not value-neutral: oldCash is EconomicValue
         7 and casinoCoin is 5, so a 1:1 swap by count is about 29% less purchasing power than the
         old numbers implied. Set the vending prices against the real figure below, not against
         the old cash amounts.

             Dukes per sweep after this change: 953

         SCALES WITH THE SAFES. There are ten safes now and the plan is one helper in every room,
         so the safe contribution is 43.4 Dukes per safe per restock and the total climbs with the
         room count rather than staying put. Worth re-reading once the safes are all in: at sixty
         rooms the safes alone are about 2,600 a sweep, and on the two-day respawn that is a very
         different economy from this one. The dial, if it needs one, is the loot_prob_template on
         groupSmallSafeLoot03, not this line.

         WHY setattribute AND NOT A LIST OF APPENDS. Changing the name attribute in place keeps
         vanilla's own counts, probabilities and quality templates exactly as they are, so the
         distribution of the money is untouched and only the denomination changes. Appending
         casinoCoin entries alongside would have doubled the drops instead of converting them.
         ============================================================ -->
    <setattribute xpath="//item[@name='oldCash']" name="name">casinoCoin</setattribute>

    <!-- ============================================================
         THE CHECK-IN GUESTS' BAGS (v1.5.4, FIXED IN v1.5.5 AND AGAIN IN v1.5.6)

         Five bags, one per bag class in entityclasses.xml. What a guest was carrying when they
         walked into the lobby, so the contents say who they were rather than being generic
         salvage. Nothing here is construction material: the building supplies that, these are
         personal effects.

         DUKES ARE IN EVERY BAG and that is the point. Vending machines are the hotel's only shop
         and they sell rather than buy, so Dukes are the one currency the run has. A wallet is the
         most honest thing a guest can be carrying.

         ==== THE v1.5.4 BREAKAGE, RECORDED IN FULL BECAUSE IT WAS ENTIRELY SELF-INFLICTED ====

         v1.5.4 shipped with count="all" on the LOOTCONTAINER. That is not a legal value there and
         it took the WHOLE FILE down:

             ERR XML loader: Loading and parsing 'loot.xml' failed
             EXC Parsing error count (input='all')

         One bad attribute in an appended block means the armoury, the safe lists and the
         oldCash-to-Dukes conversion all silently stopped existing. A loot.xml error is never
         local to the thing you just added.

         The shape is now vanilla's own, counted rather than assumed: across the whole of the
         game's loot.xml, count="all" appears on <lootgroup> 361 times and on <lootcontainer>
         ZERO times. A bag is a container of count="1" holding ONE group, and the group carries
         count="all" and the items. That is exactly zPackReg -> groupZpackReg.

         HOW THIS WENT WRONG TWICE IN ONE BUILD is the part worth keeping. The first draft
         invented the sounds (open_bag, which does not exist) and used count="2,3", which would
         have rolled only two or three entries so a bag could contain no money at all. Catching
         that, I "corrected" count to "all" — and invented again instead of reading zPackReg
         properly the second time. Both errors were the same act: writing what seemed reasonable
         instead of copying what the game already does.

         ==== THE v1.5.5 BREAKAGE, WHICH WAS THE SAME MISTAKE AGAIN ====

         v1.5.5 put the groups in <append xpath="/lootgroups">. THERE IS NO SUCH PATH. The root
         element of loot.xml IS <lootcontainers>, and <lootgroup> and <lootcontainer> are both
         DIRECT CHILDREN of it: 1015 groups and 339 containers, siblings, in one flat list. So the
         append matched nothing, the five groups were never added, and the containers then
         referenced groups that did not exist:

             EXC lootgroup 'groupOccBagHoldall' does not exist or has not been defined before
                 being reference by lootcontainer/lootgroup name='occBagHoldall'

         Which is the exact failure the armoury comment at the top of this file already warns
         about, and the working pattern was already three sections above: the room safes use
         <append xpath="/lootcontainers">. Invented a path instead of reading the file being
         edited.

         GROUPS ARE DEFINED BEFORE THEY ARE REFERENCED. The loader parses in document order, so
         both the groups and the containers go in ONE /lootcontainers append, groups first.

         EVERY ITEM ID CHECKED against the game's items.xml. Three that do NOT exist and were
         reached for first: drinkJarWater (it is drinkJarBoiledWater or drinkJarPureMineralWater),
         medicalPainkillers (it is drugPainkillers) and drinkCanBeer (it is drinkJarBeer). Vanilla
         has no purse, wallet, phone or jewellery item, so "personal effects" is carried by the
         CONTENTS rather than by flavour props.

         COUNTS ARE DELIBERATELY SMALL. A bag is a pocket, not a chest. The reward for a night's
         fighting is two or three bags, not two or three hauls. The casinoCoin line in each group
         carries no prob, so with count="all" it is guaranteed; everything else is a chance on top.
         ============================================================ -->
    <append xpath="/lootcontainers">

        <!-- The ordinary guest. A weekend bag: money, something to eat, something to drink. -->
        <lootgroup name="groupOccBagHoldall" count="all">
            <item name="casinoCoin" count="25,90"/>
            <item name="foodCanChili" count="1" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="foodCanPeas" count="1" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="drinkJarPureMineralWater" count="1,2" loot_prob_template="med" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="resourceCloth" count="2,5" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="drugVitamins" count="1" loot_prob_template="low" force_prob="true"/>
        </lootgroup>

        <!-- The businessman. A briefcase: more money, paperwork, a drink for the room. -->
        <lootgroup name="groupOccBagBriefcase" count="all">
            <item name="casinoCoin" count="60,180"/>
            <item name="resourcePaper" count="3,8" loot_prob_template="medHigh" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="drinkJarBeer" count="1" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="drinkJarCoffee" count="1" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="resourceLockPick" count="1" loot_prob_template="veryLow" force_prob="true"/>
        </lootgroup>

        <!-- The party girl. A handbag: cash, painkillers, something to keep going on. -->
        <lootgroup name="groupOccBagHandbag" count="all">
            <item name="casinoCoin" count="40,140"/>
            <item name="drugPainkillers" count="1,2" loot_prob_template="med" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="drinkCanMegaCrush" count="1" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="medicalBandage" count="1,2" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="resourceSewingKit" count="1" loot_prob_template="veryLow" force_prob="true"/>
        </lootgroup>

        <!-- Janitor and utility worker. Staff, not guests, but they still had their kit on them. -->
        <lootgroup name="groupOccBagToolbag" count="all">
            <item name="casinoCoin" count="15,50"/>
            <item name="resourceDuctTape" count="1,3" loot_prob_template="med" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="resourceMechanicalParts" count="1,4" loot_prob_template="med" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="resourceElectricParts" count="1,4" loot_prob_template="med" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="resourceOil" count="1,2" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="resourceSpring" count="1,2" loot_prob_template="low" force_prob="true"/>
        </lootgroup>

        <!-- The nurse. The one bag worth going out of your way for. -->
        <lootgroup name="groupOccBagMedkit" count="all">
            <item name="casinoCoin" count="20,60"/>
            <item name="medicalFirstAidBandage" count="1,2" loot_prob_template="medHigh" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="medicalBandage" count="2,4" loot_prob_template="med" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="drugPainkillers" count="1,2" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="drugAntibiotics" count="1" loot_prob_template="low" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="medicalSplint" count="1" loot_prob_template="low" force_prob="true"/>
        </lootgroup>

        <!-- THE SOLDIER'S KITBAG (v1.55.0). Fril: "I killed a few soldiers last night and the
             loot seemed to be more medical related that ammo and weapons". He was right, and
             the cause was not the contents: occBagWeapons had no loot list of its own and its
             LootList pointed at occBagHoldall, so the kitbag had been pouring out tinned food,
             water, cloth and VITAMINS since the day it was added. The vitamins are the medical
             item he saw. There was never any ammo in it to find.

             Ammo leads by a clear margin, with one field dressing because a soldier carrying a
             dressing is right and one line does not make it a medkit. Item names were checked
             against vanilla items.xml rather than typed from memory: resourceBrass and
             armorMilitaryVest do NOT exist.

             v1.56.0, Fril: "lose the resourceScrapBrass ... add weapons parts instead. Reduce
             the amount of ammo762mmBulletBall 5-10 (they wont have an AK for ages so giving
             them loads early will just fill the inventory. It also makes the 300 in the loot
             room worthless if they already have 300 from looting bags and safes." 7.62 is
             therefore 5-10 rather than 10-30: the loot room's stash has to stay worth finding,
             and a bag that hands out ammo for a gun the player cannot have yet is just
             inventory clutter. -->
        <lootgroup name="groupOccBagWeapons" count="all">
            <item name="casinoCoin" count="20,70"/>
            <item name="ammo9mmBulletBall" count="15,40" loot_prob_template="medHigh" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="ammo762mmBulletBall" count="5,10" loot_prob_template="med" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="ammoShotgunShell" count="6,16" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <!-- v1.56.0: parts in place of the scrap brass Fril cut. ONE T1 part per ammo type
                 already in the bag, so the kitbag reads as one soldier's kit rather than a
                 random parts bin. Vanilla's own groupWeapons_RangedParts was rejected: it
                 carries rocket launcher and robotics parts, which is exactly the early-game
                 flooding this change exists to avoid. count 1,2 is vanilla's conservative
                 figure from its weaponParts group, not invented here. -->
            <item name="gunHandgunT1PistolParts" count="1,2" loot_prob_template="medLow" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="gunShotgunT1DoubleBarrelParts" count="1,2" loot_prob_template="low" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="gunRifleT1HuntingRifleParts" count="1,2" loot_prob_template="low" force_prob="true"/>
            <item name="medicalFirstAidBandage" count="1" loot_prob_template="low" force_prob="true"/>
        </lootgroup>

        <!-- THE BOOK BAG (v1.5.8). Books and nothing else: no Dukes, no food, no parts. It is the
             one bag that is not about who the guest was, so it carries none of their belongings.
             skillMagazines is vanilla's own pool and carries abundance_type="Magazines", so the
             sandbox MagazinesCountModifier still scales it per tier, which is correct. -->
        <lootgroup name="groupOccBagBooks" count="all">
            <item group="skillMagazines" count="1,3"/>
            <item group="perkBooks" count="1" loot_prob_template="low" force_prob="true"/>
            <!-- v1.14.0: one guaranteed essential (workstation / electrical / vehicle). The
                 group is count="all" and this line carried no prob, so it ALWAYS fired.
                 Declared inline rather than xpath-appended because occEssentialMags and this
                 group are both ours, defined in this same file.

                 v1.96.0: NO LONGER GUARANTEED. Fril: "instead of a guaranteed drop from this we
                 have a 33% chance that 1,3 of those magazines are in the book bag."

                 WHY IT MATTERED. Every one of the 25 guest classes drops bags on a 6:4 split, so
                 exactly 40% of every kill in the hotel was a Book Bag, and every one of those
                 carried a guaranteed essential magazine. Two kills in five handed over a
                 workstation, electrical or vehicle magazine with no roll involved. That is a
                 progression tap rather than loot, and it sits badly with this file's own
                 position that Area 7's "leave the magazines alone" call does not transfer here
                 because "the magazines are not the point in a hotel".

                 A raw prob rather than a loot_prob_template, matching occSafeFirst's lockpick
                 line in this same file. Templates scale with game stage; this should not.

                 THE 6:4 BAG WEIGHTING IS UNCHANGED, so the Book Bag is still 40% of drops. Only
                 what is inside it has moved. -->
            <item group="occEssentialMags" count="1,3" prob="0.33"/>
        </lootgroup>



        <!-- THE FOB BAG (v1.9.0). Everything here is GUARANTEED: no loot_prob_template on any
             line, so nothing is a roll. This is the reward for the only fight in the mod that
             cannot be avoided, and a bad roll on the key would end the run. -->
        <lootgroup name="groupOccBagFob" count="all">
            <item name="occKeyFob" count="1"/>
            <item name="ammo9mmBulletBall" count="30,60"/>
            <item name="ammo762mmBulletBall" count="20,40"/>
            <item name="drinkJarPureMineralWater" count="2,3"/>
